{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Elder Affairs to make an investigation and study of a certain current Senate document relative to community care retirement communities special commission\r\n\r\n","BillNumber":"S2722","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J44","Name":"Joint Committee on Elder Affairs","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J44","ResponseDate":"2024-04-05T13:32:20.207"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2722/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, April 16, 2024 -- The committee on  Elder Affairs , to whom was referred the petition (accompanied by resolve, Senate, No. 401) of Michael F. Rush and Paul McMurtry that provisions be made for an investigation and study by a special commission relative to the regulation of continuing care retirement communities, report the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2722).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Elder Affairs be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate document numbered 401 relative to community care retirement communities special commission.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J44","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J44"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}